# E20 MasMobileConsole: one process per container in the C#, three environments on the loopback transport in the C++;
# the console of each container is compared in its own section. The lines of the C# Container class (connection to
# the server, registration, "Running MAS...") are not compared: the server and the containers are not ported, the
# transport plays their part. Parallel: the static agents start, answer and are answered in any order within a
# container; the trip, its itinerary and the report are compared in order, the information received as a multiset.
section ^This is Container\d$
ignore ^$
ignore ^Container connecting to server\.\.\.$
ignore ^Container connected to server\.$
ignore ^Container\d registered\.$
ignore ^Running MAS\.\.\.$
cover all
fact enter ^Press ENTER to start MAS in container (Container\d)$
fact static ^Static agent (\S+) starting$
fact home ^Mobile agent starting at home$
fact itinerary ^(Container\d)$
fact moving ^I'm moving to (Container\d)$
fact moved ^I have moved to (Container\d)$
fact message ^\t\[(\S+) -> (\S+)\]: (.+)$
fact report ^(Reporting:|Moving to Container\d|Arrived to Container\d|Stopping)$
fact info ^Received info: (.+)$
same enter seq
same static bag by 0
same home seq
same itinerary seq
same moving seq
same moved seq
same message bag by 0
same report seq
same info bag
check static count == 6
check message count == 12
check info count == 6
